A||N||7||dgroves||Firing order/cylinder location||||5||
Z||000000||dgroves||06-07-2001||09:57 AM||||Just purchased a car that others had attempted an engine replacement. (2.8 liter with 2.8 liter from junk yard) Botched job and now I need info. The manuals that I have access to either don't tell or they are un-clear as to the cylinder location. <P>Standing at the right rear of the car and looking at what would be the front of the engine if it was in a S-10 (Water pump end)Is the #1 cylinder on the right or left? <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Ken Wittlief||06-07-2001||10:05 AM||||standing behind the car and looking at the motor the cylinders are:<P>6 4 2<P>5 3 1<P>  and the distributor spins clock wise looking down on it, plug #1 at the 3'oclock postition, and it goes 1 2 3 4 5 6. <P>   this might be a little off if someone has pulled the dist and put it back in a tooth off. On mine #1 is more like 4'oclock than 3 - not a problem as long as the timing is set accordingly.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||06-07-2001||10:08 AM||||looked at your question again, isnt the water pump on the right side of the motor when its in a fiero?!<P> either way, when the motor is in the fiero, the cylinders are as in my last post.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||06-07-2001||01:28 PM||||To start off with, "forward" means toward the waterpump end of the engine.<P>One of the valve covers will be about half an inch forward of the other. The forward most cylinder in the forward valve cover is #1. #2 is the forward most cylinder in the other bank, etc.<P>Firing order is 1-2-3-4-5-6.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||06-07-2001||02:14 PM||||Looking at the engine from the water pump side, #1 is on the left side. #2 is on the right side. #2 is closest to the battery.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ken Wittlief||06-07-2001||02:17 PM||||Standing on an overpass, facing north, with the Fiero directly underneight you, upsidedown, in a ditch, pointing westsouthwest<P>  cylinder one is....||||reg||1
Z||000006||Will||06-07-2001||04:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR>[B]Standing on an overpass, facing north, with the Fiero directly underneight you, upsidedown, in a ditch, pointing westsouthwest<BR>B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nuthin' but net  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||StuGood||06-08-2001||06:18 PM||||Just looked at mine, and the number one cylinder was on the <B>west</B> end of the motor.<P>"Your car may vary."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>The others who posted are correct.  How's that for an easy-to-remember firing order?  So easy, sometimes people don't believe me when I mention it.  As if I would kid anyone! :;    <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by dgroves:<BR><B>Just purchased a car that others had attempted an engine replacement...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Come to think of it, if they <B>really</B> botched the engine replacement, I suppose the number one cylinder could end up almost anywhere.  <BR>||||reg||12
